      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.71,
      "end_seconds": 9.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "so, no problem at all, come in what's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.17,
      "end_seconds": 22.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "I'm here because of a sore throat work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.47,
      "end_seconds": 30.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.52,
      "end_seconds": 36.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Severe, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.41,
      "end_seconds": 40.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.74,
      "end_seconds": 50.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "it usually comes with swollen glands in my neck. About swollen glands in my neck, mild, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.68,
      "end_seconds": 55.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "what about a fever, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.22,
      "end_seconds": 62.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "mm yes. As for fever only paracetamol and it's not much"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.2,
      "end_seconds": 80.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Have you had any cough or trouble opening the mouth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.46,
      "end_seconds": 87.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "I haven't had cough or trouble opening the mouth no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.42,
      "end_seconds": 93.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "have you had any ear pain rash or drooling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.32,
      "end_seconds": 99.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "I haven't had ear pain rash or drooling no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.58,
      "end_seconds": 105.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Alright have you noticed any weakness or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.32,
      "end_seconds": 108.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.09,
      "end_seconds": 117.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record? Bear with me I'm just building up the the picture"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.44,
      "end_seconds": 128.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "I've had thin bones for two years now. I've had an irregular heartbeat for two years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.73,
      "end_seconds": 136.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "right, right can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.27,
      "end_seconds": 147.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "it's alendronate 70 milligrams once a week i take bisoprolol 2.5 milligrams once a day for the heart rhythm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.41,
      "end_seconds": 157.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.4,
      "end_seconds": 162.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.66,
      "end_seconds": 165.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.76,
      "end_seconds": 171.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.03,
      "end_seconds": 175.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.87,
      "end_seconds": 180.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.03,
      "end_seconds": 193.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.68,
      "end_seconds": 195.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "no never"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.4,
      "end_seconds": 200.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.1,
      "end_seconds": 215.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.05,
      "end_seconds": 240.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "okay: oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temp 38.8 degrees, blood pressure 105 over 70, pulse is 89 beats a minute"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.27,
      "end_seconds": 246.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.16,
      "end_seconds": 249.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.32,
      "end_seconds": 275.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "both tonsils are red and enlarged with white patches, and the the neck glands are tender"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.56,
      "end_seconds": 291.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.09,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Okay thinking it through this looks most like tonsillitis. I want to be honest that this is an impression not a final answer. We shouldn't forget glandular fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.29,
      "end_seconds": 295.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.11,
      "end_seconds": 306.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.5,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now tonsillitis is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want a throat swab done, that's for sore throat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 307.97,
      "end_seconds": 312.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "we have a slot Friday at 2 pm, if that works"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.82,
      "end_seconds": 315.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "okay I'll be there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.26,
      "end_seconds": 342.35,
      "duration_seconds": 25.09,
      "text": "I'm going to put you on phenoxymethylpenicillin 500 milligrams four times a day for ten days. That's for tonsillitis. Gargle with warm salt water and drink plenty of fluids. The thing that would worry me is if you cannot swallow your saliva or have trouble breathing. If that happens go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.82,
      "end_seconds": 346.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Yes I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.17,
      "end_seconds": 356.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "book a review if it isn't better in three days. I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.83,
      "end_seconds": 359.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
